of just how important this really is.

18
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.799
It saves memory overhead unnecessarily compiling your shaders and allows you to swap out

19
00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:20.939
textures and values quickly, not recompiling the material continually.

20
00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:24.540
Shader stuttering is a big issue when it comes to making your game.

21
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:29.540
Some of the things that can help prevent that from happening is one, packing your RGB

22
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.500
into your textures when you can.

23
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.620
And I showed you that in the beginning of our course.

24
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:40.239
Make fewer parent materials, limiting unique materials with dependencies and use material

25
00:01:40.239 --> 00:01:44.859
instancing as much as possible, which we just talked about.

26
00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:50.060
You also want to manage shaders with complexity such as translucency and not have too many

27
